hello everyone this is Satoru Iwata from  Nintendo Satoru Iwata story is one laced  with unbelievable risks bright thinking  and dark times and a bold ambition to  make a difference for all that can be  said about his charming mannerisms his  warm smile his unquestionable love of  video games it should not be overlooked  they owatta was a visionary businessman  who saved Nintendo by reinventing it he  was a radical force a revolutionary  figure who commanded a century-old  company as though it was his own startup  foreseeing a bleak future in retreading  old ground it were to took Nintendo down  the Uncharted path often with its future  hinging on little more than his peculiar  ideas those who believed in him were  rewarded with the most prosperous period  in the corporations proud history even  it was his appointment to the head of  Nintendo in 2002 was unconventional by  Nature  he was the company's very first elected  president who had no blood ties to the  Yamaguchi's the family that had founded  and managed in Tendo across three  generations his promotion came a bleak  hour for Nintendo with the Gamecube  languishing in the shadow of the  PlayStation 2 with retailers and  publishers abandoning the console little  more than a year into his tenure the  water had to warn investors that the  corporation had begun losing money but  in the same speech where he announced in  tendo's first half fiscal loss it were  to revealed plans for a new system that  would take the company on a bold new  direction the Nintendo DS was his first  major gamble a bizarre-looking handheld  that housed two separate screens in a  clamshell design it was the first  mainstream games platform to use a  touchscreen and stylus and one that  clearly prioritized how it felt over how  it looked the secret to the ds's  record-breaking sales was neither how it  played or looked however its success was  down to irritants belief that he could  ignite interest in people who didn't  typically play games so for every new  Super Mario Brothers and Mario Kart vs  released for the handheld there was also  the daily mental workout companion Brain  Age and the virtual pet simulator  Nintendogs the DS which underwent  several revisions throughout its 10  years on the market sold more than 150  million  it's Nintendo's handheld business which  some felt was doomed by the arrival of  Sony's PlayStation Portable had become  more prosperous than ever  even before the reveal of the Nintendo  DS at e3 2004 it was already had bigger  and bolder plans in place he said the  handheld should serve as a hint towards  our next-generation console but if you  would have predicted how far it was it  was prepared to go the second major  gamble the Wii was so radical so  implausibly different that it belongs in  a league of its own  rather taking a game show in September  2005 it were to took the stage and held  up a bizarre one-handed game controller  this was perhaps the defining moment of  his career a wild and arguably reckless  break from more than 30 years of  tradition what followed TGS 2005 was a  frenzy a fever of debate and speculation  and unforgettable excitement It was as  though the audience didn't know how to  react mr. Iwata said of his Tokyo Game  Show reveal while there were significant  reservations from some fans the sheer  enigma of the we had captured the  imagination of the gaming world the  console became the fastest-selling in  history brought games to entirely new  audiences and ushered in a new age of  motion control it would never reach that  height again the 3ds initially struggled  with a lukewarm reception to its  stereoscopic 3d as well as a declining  market handhelds for the Wii U is more  clear-cut failure another brave idea  certainly the one that did not connect  with the masses Nintendo like all  creative companies will stumble again  and again throughout its lifetime that  is a natural floor of any person or  company that dares to innovate that  dares to expose itself where Nintendo is  undoubtedly standing on far more solid  foundations now than it was 13 years ago  it was his legacy serves as a reminder  of how far one can go  if they never give up on their ideas  [Music]  on my business card I am a corporate  president in my mind I am a game  developer but in my heart I am a gamer  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

